{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>These sinners against their own souls.</b> They became rebellious against their own souls — for they split with the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>Beaten plates.</b> Thin sheets." "<b>Plates.</b> Beaten-flat plates; טינדי״ש בלע״ז." "<b>A covering for the altar.</b> For the bronze altar." "<b>And they shall be a sign.</b> For a memorial — so that they would say: these were from those who split over the priesthood and were burned."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French tendille, a type of thin metal plate"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:21.344998702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}